  "description": "The 48 White Mountain peaks of New Hampshire that reach 4,000 feet, the classic AMC peak-bagging list.",
  "criteria": "Summits at least 4,000 ft with at least 200 ft of rise on all sides (prominence rule), as defined by the AMC. Wildcat A and Wildcat D, the North and South Kinsman, North and South Hancock, East Osceola, and North/Middle Tripyramid count as separate peaks.",
  "organization": "AMC Four Thousand Footer Committee",
  "officialUrl": "https://amc4000footer.org/",
  "notes": "AMC winter rules: a winter ascent counts only if the entire hike starts after the winter solstice and ends before the spring equinox (astronomical/calendar winter); the hike must start and end within that window. Owl's Head and Isolation are remote, and Owl's Head is trailless. Tecumseh was resurveyed in 2019 at about 3,997 ft but remains on the AMC list. Elevations follow 4000footers.com.",
